<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Self-elevating unit monitoring — early-warning demonstrator</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="../_assets/brand.css">
<style>
  .wrap{max-width:var(--wrap);margin:0 auto;padding:20px clamp(14px,3vw,32px) 40px}
  header{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:flex-start;gap:18px;flex-wrap:wrap}
  h1{font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);color:var(--brand);margin:10px 0}
  h2{font-size:20px;color:var(--brand)} h3{font-size:16px;color:var(--brand)}
  a{color:var(--accent)} .muted{color:var(--muted)}
  .card{background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--edge);border-radius:var(--r);box-shadow:var(--shadow);padding:18px;margin:16px 0}
  .controls{display:flex;gap:22px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap}
  .scrub{flex:1;min-width:220px} input[type=range]{width:100%;accent-color:var(--accent)}
  select,button{font:inherit;background:var(--panel-2);color:var(--ink);border:1px solid var(--edge);border-radius:8px;padding:8px}
  :focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--accent);outline-offset:3px}
  #status{border-left:5px solid var(--accent);padding:10px 14px;font-weight:650}
  #status[data-alert="true"]{border-color:#b75d00}
  svg{width:100%;height:auto;display:block;color:var(--muted)}
  .plots{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,450px),1fr));gap:16px}
  .plots .card{margin:0} .readout{min-height:2.5em;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
  .table-wrap{overflow:auto} table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14px}
  td,th{text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--edge);padding:10px}
  th{color:var(--brand)} #mapping{min-width:1100px} li{margin:12px 0}
  .legend{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted)} .c1{color:#2477b3}.c2{color:#00877b}
  footer{border-top:1px solid var(--edge);margin-top:24px;padding-top:14px;color:var(--muted)}
  @media print{.controls,#theme{display:none}.card{box-shadow:none}.table-wrap{overflow:visible}#mapping{min-width:0}}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main class="wrap">
<header>
  <div><a href="short-horizon-motion-forecast.html">Marine operations · motion forecast</a>
  <h1>Self-elevating unit monitoring</h1>
  <p class="muted">Liftboats and jack-ups · which instrument catches each failure mode early?</p></div>
  <button id="theme" type="button" aria-label="Toggle colour theme">Theme</button>
</header>
<section class="card" aria-labelledby="summary-title">
  <h2 id="summary-title">Summary</h2>
  <p>Preload settlement that stops is compared with settlement that accelerates. In the elevated-storm example, leg inclination and strain rise toward illustrative limits. The instrument table connects six failure modes to observable precursors, explicit alert inputs and conditional lead times.</p>
  <p><strong>Synthetic demonstration only.</strong> The mappings are engineering proposals based on the open literature below. The sources support mechanisms and measured quantities; they do not validate these warning algorithms or thresholds. No measured, client or earlier study data is used.</p>
  <p><a href="short-horizon-motion-forecast.html">The motion-forecast demonstrator</a> shows phase-resolved seconds ahead within a predictable wave zone. Qualified metocean forecasts can provide hours for preparation; monitoring confirms the response as it happens. This page does not connect to a forecast feed.</p>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="revision-title">
  <h2 id="revision-title">Revision history</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Revision</th><th>Date</th><th>What changed and why</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody><tr><td>0</td><td>2026-10-27</td><td>Initial synthetic instrument and warning demonstrator to connect observed response with advance planning.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="replay-title">
  <h2 id="replay-title">Synthetic log replay</h2>
  <div class="card controls">
    <label for="scenario">Evaluated log <select id="scenario"><option value="accelerating">Accelerating preload</option><option value="settled">Settled preload</option><option value="storm">Elevated storm</option></select></label>
    <div class="scrub"><label for="cursor">Replay time <output id="clock" for="cursor">0.0 min</output></label><input id="cursor" type="range" min="0" max="90" step="1" value="0"></div>
  </div>
  <p class="muted">Move the time slider, or point across a plot. Full traces show the constructed outcome retrospectively; the status uses only warnings confirmed by the selected time. Blue and teal distinguish the preload logs; amber marks warnings, red the imposed event and dotted purple the replay time.</p>
  <p id="status" role="status" aria-live="polite">No configured alert at 0.0 min. This is not a safety verdict.</p>
  <div id="plots" class="plots"></div>
  <noscript><p>Enable JavaScript for the interactive replay. The warning summary, settings, instrument table and sources below remain available.</p></noscript>
</section>
<section class="card" aria-labelledby="warning-title">
  <h2 id="warning-title">Warning lead time in these constructed logs</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Log</th><th>Confirmed warning</th><th>Warning time (min)</th><th>First event or limit (min)</th><th>Lead time (min)</th></tr></thead><tbody>
@@SUMMARY@@
  </tbody></table></div>
  <p>Lead time is the separately imposed event time minus the first confirming alert time. It is measured after construction of the log, not predicted by the monitor. Both storm alerts precede the first sampled response limit. A real sudden failure may have no precursor and zero lead time.</p>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="inputs-title">
  <h2 id="inputs-title">Explicit demonstration inputs</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Log</th><th>Rule</th><th>Metric</th><th>Threshold</th><th>Consecutive samples</th><th>Maximum sample gap</th></tr></thead><tbody>
@@RULES@@
  </tbody></table></div>
  <p>Preload is sampled every 10.0 s; it ramps to 1000.0 kN at 4.0 min and then holds. Both logs start with exponentially decaying settlement. The accelerating log adds quadratic penetration after the hold begins, followed by an imposed jump at 11.0 min. The storm is sampled every 60.0 s with linearly increasing inclination and strain; illustrative limits are 450.0 mdeg and 1200.0 µε. Inclination is plotted in millidegrees (1000.0 mdeg = 1.0 deg).</p>
  <p>Each rule requires a channel, metric, threshold, unit, persistence and maximum gap. Magnitude uses absolute values; rise rate and acceleration retain their sign, with positive settlement downward. Backward differences use actual elapsed time, with acceleration between interval midpoints. Equality counts as a crossing; a non-crossing sample resets persistence. Confirmation is timestamped at the final required sample. Invalid values, missing channels and excessive gaps raise an error: the monitor is unavailable, not safe.</p>
  <p>All settings and synthetic formulas are declared in <code>digitalmodel.marine_ops.self_elevating_monitoring</code>. Use <code>evaluate(time_s, channels, rules)</code> with caller-supplied settings and consistent units. Preload rules apply only to the selected loading phase; a real adapter must confirm the preload hold. No automatic hold detection, sensor ingestion or unit conversion is implemented.</p>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="mapping-title">
  <h2 id="mapping-title">Failure modes and instrument selection</h2>
  <p>Typical alert forms below require site-specific values. Lead-time descriptions are conditional engineering estimates, not published guarantees or recommended operating margins.</p>
  <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Instrument mapping table, scroll horizontally"><table id="mapping"><thead><tr><th>Failure mode</th><th>Instruments</th><th>Precursor signal</th><th>Explicit alert logic inputs</th><th>Time potentially available</th><th>Open source basis</th></tr></thead><tbody>
@@MAPPINGS@@
  </tbody></table></div>
</section>
<section class="card" aria-labelledby="limits-title">
  <h2 id="limits-title">Limits and way forward</h2>
  <p>Soil layering, foundation capacity, structural utilization, sliding resistance, overturning margin and intact or damaged stability are not solved. IMU attitude does not measure stability reserve; inclination and strain alone cannot reliably detect pure sliding. A position reference, load assessment and geotechnical investigation are needed. The wave experiment cited below supports displacement and acceleration monitoring, not a field warning performance claim.</p>
  <p>Before field use, the maintainer should obtain site and equipment assessments, survey references, sensor calibration and temperature compensation, clock synchronization, noise filtering, data-quality alarms and independent protective trips. Set thresholds below assessed limits with sufficient time for the approved response; qualify them on representative logs and a holdout set. A warning calls for review under approved procedures. No configured alert is not permission to continue.</p>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="sources-title">
  <h2 id="sources-title">Open literature and public guidance</h2>
  <p>Sources were retrieved on 2026-10-27. Only paraphrased physical mechanisms and monitoring proposals are included; numerical limits from licensed standards are not reproduced. The journal articles provide the mechanism basis. Strain, inclination and drive-load warning rules are proposed engineering extensions, not algorithms validated by those articles. The federal regulations address liftboats; they are context for the demonstrator, not a claim of applicability to every jack-up.</p>
  <ol>
@@SOURCES@@
  </ol>
</section>
<footer>Generated from the table-driven monitoring module. Reproduce with <code>PYTHONPATH=src python scripts/capabilities/build_self_elevating_monitoring.py</code>. No external plotting scripts or network requests are used by this page.</footer>
</main>
<script id="monitor-data" type="application/json">@@DATA@@</script>
<script>
"use strict";
const cases = JSON.parse(document.getElementById("monitor-data").textContent);
const scenario = document.getElementById("scenario");
const cursor = document.getElementById("cursor");
const colors = ["#2477b3", "#00877b"];
const fmt = value => Number(value).toFixed(1);

function plot(chart, data, now) {
  const w = 800, h = 260, left = 72, right = 22, top = 60, bottom = 42;
  const tmax = data.time_s[data.time_s.length - 1];
  const ymax = Math.max(1, chart.limit || 0, chart.threshold || 0,
    ...chart.traces.flatMap(trace => trace.values)) * 1.12;
  const x = t => left + t / tmax * (w-left-right);
  const y = v => h-bottom - v / ymax * (h-top-bottom);
  let svg = `<svg viewBox="0 0 ${w} ${h}" role="img" aria-label="${chart.title}: ${chart.unit} against time in minutes"><title>${chart.title}</title>`;
  for (let i=0;i<=4;i++) {
    const v = ymax*i/4, t=tmax*i/4;
    svg += `<path d="M${left},${y(v)}H${w-right}" stroke="currentColor" opacity=".15"/>`;
    svg += `<text x="${left-8}" y="${y(v)+4}" fill="currentColor" text-anchor="end" font-size="12">${fmt(v)}</text>`;
    svg += `<text x="${x(t)}" y="${h-20}" fill="currentColor" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12">${fmt(t/60)}</text>`;
  }
  svg += `<text x="${left}" y="18" fill="currentColor" font-size="13">${chart.unit}</text><text x="${w-right}" y="${h-2}" fill="currentColor" text-anchor="end" font-size="12">Time (min)</text>`;
  for (const [index, trace] of chart.traces.entries()) {
    const path = trace.values.map((v,i) => `${i ? "L" : "M"}${x(data.time_s[i])},${y(v)}`).join(" ");
    svg += `<path d="${path}" fill="none" stroke="${colors[index]}" stroke-width="2.5"/>`;
  }
  for (const [field,label,color] of [["threshold","Warning threshold","#b75d00"],["limit","Response limit","#bd2636"]]) {
    if (chart[field] !== undefined) {
      svg += `<path d="M${left},${y(chart[field])}H${w-right}" stroke="${color}" stroke-dasharray="6 4"/>`;
      svg += `<text x="${w-right}" y="${y(chart[field])-5}" text-anchor="end" fill="${color}" font-size="12">${label}: ${fmt(chart[field])}</text>`;
    }
  }
  for (const [index,alert] of data.alerts.entries()) {
    svg += `<path d="M${x(alert.time_s)},${top}V${h-bottom}" stroke="#b75d00" stroke-dasharray="5 4"/>`;
    svg += `<text x="${left+index*270}" y="${34+index*16}" fill="#b75d00" font-size="12">${alert.rule}: ${fmt(alert.time_s/60)} min</text>`;
  }
  if (data.event_s !== null) {
    svg += `<path d="M${x(data.event_s)},${top}V${h-bottom}" stroke="#bd2636" stroke-width="2"/>`;
    svg += `<text x="${w-right}" y="18" text-anchor="end" fill="#bd2636" font-size="12">Event: ${fmt(data.event_s/60)} min</text>`;
  }
  return svg + `<path d="M${x(now)},${top}V${h-bottom}" stroke="#9055bf" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="2 3"/></svg>`;
}

function render() {
  const data = cases[scenario.value];
  cursor.max = data.time_s.length-1;
  const index = Math.min(Number(cursor.value), data.time_s.length-1);
  cursor.value = index;
  const now = data.time_s[index];
  document.getElementById("clock").textContent = `${fmt(now/60)} min`;
  const alerts = data.alerts.filter(alert => alert.time_s <= now);
  const status = document.getElementById("status");
  status.dataset.alert = String(alerts.length > 0);
  const event = data.event_s !== null && now >= data.event_s ? " Synthetic event reached." : "";
  status.textContent = alerts.length ? `Confirmed: ${alerts.map(a=>a.rule).join("; ")}.${event}` : "No configured alert. This is not a safety verdict.";
  const plots = document.getElementById("plots");
  plots.innerHTML = data.charts.map(chart => `<article class="card"><h3>${chart.title}</h3><p class="legend">${chart.traces.map((trace,i)=>`<span class="c${i+1}">${trace.label}</span>`).join(" · ")}</p>${plot(chart,data,now)}<p class="readout">${chart.traces.map(trace=>`${trace.label}: ${fmt(trace.values[index])} ${chart.unit}`).join(" · ")}</p></article>`).join("");
  for (const svg of plots.querySelectorAll("svg")) {
    svg.addEventListener("pointermove", event => {
      const box = svg.getBoundingClientRect();
      const fraction = ((event.clientX-box.left)/box.width*800-72)/(800-72-22);
      const next = Math.round(Math.max(0,Math.min(1,fraction))*(data.time_s.length-1));
      if (Number(cursor.value) !== next) { cursor.value = next; render(); }
    });
  }
}
scenario.addEventListener("change", () => { cursor.value=0; render(); });
cursor.addEventListener("input", render);
document.getElementById("theme").addEventListener("click", () => {
  const root = document.documentElement;
  const dark = root.dataset.theme ? root.dataset.theme === "dark" : matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)").matches;
  root.dataset.theme = dark ? "light" : "dark";
});
render();
</script>
</body>
</html>
